[{:db/id 17592186087772 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-47a2dcc0-e258-5962-a656-0d85d7377a49"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087773 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b7f674b2-aab8-52eb-92a0-8e6f21742e6b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087774 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f8f7ce6d-af6c-546a-90a8-f18d93a76742"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087594 :question/problem "Given the equation $y''+12y'+36y = 0$  for $y=y(x),$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?\n\nI. $xe^{-6x}$\n\nII. $4e^{-6x}-3xe^{-6x}$\n\nIII. $2e^{6x}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-47a2dcc0-e258-5962-a656-0d85d7377a49" :question/id #uuid "47a2dcc0-e258-5962-a656-0d85d7377a49" :question/math-academy-id "q-90877" :question/problem "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}+9y=0.$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ is a solution to the equation, then $\\lambda =$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-6\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+9{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +9) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +9 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -3)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =3$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-66bbcaef-4127-5612-b288-bf682df65c65"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-66bbcaef-4127-5612-b288-bf682df65c65" :answer-field/id #uuid "66bbcaef-4127-5612-b288-bf682df65c65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a6605268-308f-5aa9-8a2b-aea33ea5ec54" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6fb89a7-9365-52c1-965f-ef6f3b099aef" "answer-f9ccba15-05c7-5055-ad65-da81a553ece8" "answer-5dfe0d35-2b45-549e-9933-eda97f80460e" "answer-a6605268-308f-5aa9-8a2b-aea33ea5ec54" "answer-a53e8e73-9688-515a-b743-c06ba5034590"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6fb89a7-9365-52c1-965f-ef6f3b099aef" :answer/id #uuid "c6fb89a7-9365-52c1-965f-ef6f3b099aef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9ccba15-05c7-5055-ad65-da81a553ece8" :answer/id #uuid "f9ccba15-05c7-5055-ad65-da81a553ece8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5dfe0d35-2b45-549e-9933-eda97f80460e" :answer/id #uuid "5dfe0d35-2b45-549e-9933-eda97f80460e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6605268-308f-5aa9-8a2b-aea33ea5ec54" :answer/id #uuid "a6605268-308f-5aa9-8a2b-aea33ea5ec54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a53e8e73-9688-515a-b743-c06ba5034590" :answer/id #uuid "a53e8e73-9688-515a-b743-c06ba5034590" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b7f674b2-aab8-52eb-92a0-8e6f21742e6b" :question/id #uuid "b7f674b2-aab8-52eb-92a0-8e6f21742e6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130137" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +1) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +1=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -1)^{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =1$ is a repeated root.\n\nSo the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x}+Bx{e}^{x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-17496bf6-9f31-57cd-8e7d-df81c51378ec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-17496bf6-9f31-57cd-8e7d-df81c51378ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "17496bf6-9f31-57cd-8e7d-df81c51378ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b4c81132-c41c-5bf0-99f6-631bbb43fd38" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e0d39602-f1f5-5e9f-a832-afc75a851baf" "answer-46cbbb4c-cb47-543a-acd8-7156e51b12bc" "answer-47c4a9bf-3526-5449-afb6-bee6b3f978ef" "answer-8417cb9c-2a17-5b03-ae26-d7eed71a77d6" "answer-b4c81132-c41c-5bf0-99f6-631bbb43fd38"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0d39602-f1f5-5e9f-a832-afc75a851baf" :answer/id #uuid "e0d39602-f1f5-5e9f-a832-afc75a851baf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46cbbb4c-cb47-543a-acd8-7156e51b12bc" :answer/id #uuid "46cbbb4c-cb47-543a-acd8-7156e51b12bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47c4a9bf-3526-5449-afb6-bee6b3f978ef" :answer/id #uuid "47c4a9bf-3526-5449-afb6-bee6b3f978ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}+Bx{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8417cb9c-2a17-5b03-ae26-d7eed71a77d6" :answer/id #uuid "8417cb9c-2a17-5b03-ae26-d7eed71a77d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4c81132-c41c-5bf0-99f6-631bbb43fd38" :answer/id #uuid "b4c81132-c41c-5bf0-99f6-631bbb43fd38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{x}+Bx{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f8f7ce6d-af6c-546a-90a8-f18d93a76742" :question/id #uuid "f8f7ce6d-af6c-546a-90a8-f18d93a76742" :question/math-academy-id "q-90967" :question/problem "Given the equation ${y}^{″}-10{y}^{′}+25y=0$ for $y=y(x),$ which of the following is **not** a solution to this equation?" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-10\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+25{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +25) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +25 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -5)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =5$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation.\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{5x}$ and $x{e}^{5x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only ${e}^{5x}-5{e}^{x}$ is not a solution." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6361ce30-11cc-5a0d-850d-da69a68b03ec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6361ce30-11cc-5a0d-850d-da69a68b03ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "6361ce30-11cc-5a0d-850d-da69a68b03ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-47d65475-b294-5939-87f4-976439c24d81" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ef346c19-c04f-532b-9394-8e47cdeef76c" "answer-166df338-5ee1-5ac6-aaaa-9ca285549f5a" "answer-f211fd22-4438-5855-a248-834360be2359" "answer-47d65475-b294-5939-87f4-976439c24d81" "answer-a95b7289-0f33-518d-a65d-3efd954fb420"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef346c19-c04f-532b-9394-8e47cdeef76c" :answer/id #uuid "ef346c19-c04f-532b-9394-8e47cdeef76c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-x{e}^{5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-166df338-5ee1-5ac6-aaaa-9ca285549f5a" :answer/id #uuid "166df338-5ee1-5ac6-aaaa-9ca285549f5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f211fd22-4438-5855-a248-834360be2359" :answer/id #uuid "f211fd22-4438-5855-a248-834360be2359" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{5x}+5x{e}^{5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47d65475-b294-5939-87f4-976439c24d81" :answer/id #uuid "47d65475-b294-5939-87f4-976439c24d81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{5x}-5{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a95b7289-0f33-518d-a65d-3efd954fb420" :answer/id #uuid "a95b7289-0f33-518d-a65d-3efd954fb420" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{5x}-x{e}^{5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087944 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
